\begin{abstract}
ASCE-RADEM v4.0 is a unified computational architecture integrating 
exascale high-performance computing, post-quantum cryptographic telemetry 
ingestion, and non-Euclidean geodesic optimal control. This article presents 
the mathematical foundations, cryptographic pipeline, control-theoretic 
framework, hardware-software co-design, and experimental benchmarks 
demonstrating real-time atmospheric simulation and control at 60 Hz across 
512 GPU compute nodes. The system provides a reproducible and scalable 
framework for secure, real-time environmental modeling and actuation.
\end{abstract}

\keywords{High-Performance Computing, Post-Quantum Cryptography, 
Geodesic Control, Atmospheric Simulation, Exascale Systems}

